    <section class="section method-section" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="section-label">05 — Method</p>
          <div class="section-title-row">
            <h2 id="method-title">The part that does not fit in a screenshot.</h2>
            <p class="section-intro">The interesting question is not whether the code compiles. It is whether the next person can trust it, change it, and ship it on a Friday.</p>
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="method-grid">
          <article class="method-card method-blue">
            <span class="method-index">01 / SPEC</span>
            <h3>Spec before code.</h3>
            <p>ODF starts with a route, a context manifest, and a gate. The goal is the right change, not the first change.</p>
